 the same area, while the Douro DOC covers still and sparkling wines and the fortified Moscatel do Douro."],"blurb":{"text":"Portugal's river valley best known for Port, though it makes about as much unfortified table wine. Allowed grapes include Rabigato and Touriga Nacional."},"study":true,"levels":[3],"sources":[{"name":"Wikidata sitelinks and Wikimedia page views","url":"https://www.wikidata.org"},{"name":"Candiago et al. 2022, A geospatial inventory of regulatory information for wine protected designations of origin in Europe, Scientific Data (product specifications as of 2021)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01513-0"},{"name":"Fick and Hijmans 2017, WorldClim 2.1 monthly averages for 1970 to 2000, 2.5 minute grid (about 4.5 km)","url":"https://www.worldclim.org/data/worldclim21.html"},{"name":"Beck et al. 2023, High-resolution (1 km) Koppen-Geiger maps, Scientific Data (1991 to 2020)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02549-6"},{"name":"Winkler, Cook, Kliewer and Lider 1974, General Viticulture, University of California Press (heat summation regions)","url":null},{"name":"Jones 2010, Climate, grapes, and wine: structure and suitability in a variable and changing climate, VIII International Terroir Congress (which grapes suit which growing season temperatures)","url":"https://ives-openscience.eu/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Climate_Grape_Wine_Jones.pdf"},{"name":"Anderson, Nelgen and Puga, Database of Regional, National and Global Winegrape Bearing Areas by Variety, 2000 to 2023, University of Adelaide (CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://doi.org/10.25909/32870405.v1"},{"name":"Wikipedia, Port wine (what the label terms mean)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Port_wine&oldid=1384891691"},{"name":"IVDP (Port and Douro Wine Institute), Circular 01/2025 (what the label term means)","url":"https://ivdp.pt/media/avlbjznd/circular_01_2025_signed_signed.pdf"},{"name":"IVDP, Sales of wines from the Douro Demarcated Region with PDO/PGI, 2025","u